  "conclusions": [
    "Aligned raw R01 source: ZSTD1 SAMPLES compressed bytes 3,414,486 vs ALP+ZSTD3 5,303,391 (~35.6% saving); staggered same value/labels: 4,126,572 vs 5,952,971 (~30.7% saving). Start-time staggering adds 31.2% physical hourly SAMPLES rows (86,688->113,760), +12.2% ALP bytes and +20.9% ZSTD1 bytes.",
    "At 8 clients, across three selectors the mean ZSTD1/ALP QueryFinish CPU ratios are ~0.982-0.993 on aligned and ~0.992-1.003 on stagger; all small effects. This supports no material global CPU win from changing codecs under 8-client CPU pressure on this 3d fixture.",
    "One-client pod_namespace ZSTD1 p50 ratio 1.003 aligned, 1.047 stagger with baseline repeated-ratio drift6.2%/7.6%; no strong interaction beyond repeat variance.",
    "One-client burst15 ZSTD1 p50 ratio 1.035 aligned vs0.942 stagger, but repeated effect drift2.7% vs8.6%; do not assert a robust sign-changing optimization without a stronger, independent repetition.",
    "All 36 panels valid at the default <=25% gate. For small effects <~5%, repeat ratio drift and A/A phase drift can exceed effect; do not label a 1-3% ratio an established global gain."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Both clock distributions are synthetic and lifecycle starts shifted without simulating correct 400-active-node population at first/final boundary, as noted in source R10.",
    "Same fixed low-entropy repetitive gauge values; high-entropy heldout is separate evidence, not part of this 2x2 stagger/concurrency test.",
    "Source ClickHouse is unoptimized O1 glibc; production allocator and optimized build not matched; no native VM comparison.",
    "All tests are read-only on OPTIMIZE FINAL single-part inner tables; no live writer, natural merges, late data, histograms, staleness, NaN/Inf, counter reset.",
    "Earlier R18 ALPZSTD3 vs ZSTD1 changes two codecs at once (ALP transform and ZSTD level); later 2x2 orthogonal factorial must isolate them.",
    "Runtime profiles sampled near request with no continuously sampled RSS; no proof of mutex contention, scheduler queue vs CPU wait separation uses exact Linux event counters."
  ],
  "next_action": "Resolve pending independent ALP transform x ZSTD(1/3) 2x2 factorial run; validate exact SAMPLES.value effective DDL, same physical schema, full native parity and controls. Do not globally promote any codec, cancel concurrent C++ build or reuse cross-runner CPU values."
}
